==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bore]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.
**1 [[I.M. Phace]] spawns.
**3 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 0.67 seconds<sup>20f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns as the boss.
**15 [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 2~2.67 seconds<sup>60f~80f</sup>.
**1 [[Bun Bun Black]] spawns.
**Infinite [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**4 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn, delay 0.67~1.33 seconds<sup>20f~40f</sup>.

==Strategy==
On paper, this enemy combination looks absolutely terrifying, until you realize that this level is split into three parts.

For the beginning phase, take advantage of the lack of pushing power. Stall Sleipnir out so you have enough cash to deal with the rest of the level, then gradually kill him once you're ready.

On your first base hit, you deal with a Bore, I.M Phace, multiple Shy Boys, and Metal Doges. This is probably the hardest part of the level. Quickly get some [[Critical Hit]]s to remove Metal Doge, using a unit like [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]], then use CC options for the Bore and use good anti-Red units as well as Area Attackers like [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] to chip both Bore and Shy Boy down.

The second base hit presents you with multiple Dark enemies and even more Metal Doges. There's really nothing more to be said here other than to just use a strong anti-Dark unit like [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl/Pizza Cat]] to deal with this, as well as getting Critical Hits on the Metal Doges.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: A decent meatshield for this stage, as he has great base health and is able to tank many hits from the Angelic Sleipnir.
*[[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]]: Great option here, because if you are able to manage the peons, he can permanently [[Freeze]] the Bun Bun Black and the Director Kurosawah and allow your cats to annihilate them.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl/Pizza Cat]]: Able to deal high damage to the Dark enemies and also deal decent damage to the rest of the peons.
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Butterfly/Fishman Cat]]: Also a very good attacker here since he easily shreds through The Faces at the start, and deals extremely high damage to the Bun Bun Black if paired with Ring Girl Cat.

